1. Frontend Hosting is done by Vercel.

The classification of Vercel is PaaS.

The reason for this classification is that Vercel provides a managed platform where the code is deployed and run.

The student does not have to manage the servers or the operating systems or the infrastructure when using Vercel.

2. Backend Hosting is also done by Vercel.

The classification of Vercel for backend hosting is also PaaS.

The reason for this classification is the same as for the frontend. Vercel manages the runtime and the scaling and the infrastructure.

The student only has to supply the application code when using Vercel for backend hosting.

3. The database used is Supabase Database.

The classification of Supabase Database is PaaS.

The reason, for this classification is that Supabase Database offers a managed PostgreSQL platform.

This platform has backups and scaling and maintenance.

The student manages the schema and the data but not the underlying database server or the infrastructure when using Supabase Database.
